        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: tighten processSchema offset/limit from Type.Number to Type.Integer",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n**Problem**: `processSchema.offset` and `processSchema.limit` accept floating-point values via `Type.Number()`, but both are inherently integer fields (line offset, line count). Float values like `offset=1.5` are silently truncated at runtime, creating an LLM intent mismatch.\n\n**Solution**: Tighten both fields to `Type.Integer()` — the schema layer now rejects floats before they reach runtime. Negative values are preserved at the schema level (no `minimum: 0` constraint) and normalized by the existing runtime guard in `sliceLogLines` (`Math.max(0, Math.floor(offset))`).\n\n**What changed / NOT changed**:\n- `src/agents/bash-tools.schemas.ts`: Two fields changed from `Type.Number` to `Type.Integer` (removed the `minimum: 0` from v1 to preserve negative-value normalization)\n- `src/agents/bash-tools.schemas.test.ts`: New focused schema validation tests covering integer acceptance, fractional rejection, and negative-value pass-through\n- No config, CLI, or public API surface changed. No dependencies added.\n\n**merge-risk declaration**: No — schema-only change to internal tool parameter types.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**After-fix test results**:\n\n```\n RUN  v4.1.9\n\n ✓ processSchema offset/limit > accepts valid integer offset and limit\n ✓ processSchema offset/limit > rejects fractional offset and limit\n ✓ processSchema offset/limit > preserves negative-value normalization — passes schema\n ✓ processSchema offset/limit > accepts omitted optional fields\n\n Test Files  2 passed (2)\n      Tests  8 passed (8)\n\n ✓ process poll waits for completion ... (8 existing tests)\n Test Files  4 passed (4)\n      Tests  24 passed (24)\n```\n\n| Input | Schema result | Runtime behavior |\n|-------|--------------|-----------------|\n| Valid integers (offset=0, limit=50) | ✅ pass | Normal processing |\n| Fractional (offset=1.5, limit=10.5) | ✅ rejected by Type.Integer | N/A |\n| Negative (offset=-1, limit=50) | ✅ pass (no minimum) | Clamped to 0 by sliceLogLines |\n| Omitted optionals | ✅ pass | Default behavior |\n\n## Risk checklist\n\n- [x] Backwards compatible — integer callers unchanged; float callers now get clear schema error; negative values preserved\n- [x] Tested with existing configurations\n- [ ] Breaking changes (if any) documented in Summary — none\n\n/cc @openclaw/clawsweeper",
        "branch": "fix/scan-20260713-1-type-number-to-integer",
